WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.601 --> 00:00:03.184
(upbeat music)

00:00:14.266 --> 00:00:17.707
- Hi, I'm Hannah I am your
friendly neighborhood wine mom,

00:00:17.707 --> 00:00:18.973
oh hi I didn't see you there.

00:00:18.973 --> 00:00:21.063
And if you are like me you believe that

00:00:21.063 --> 00:00:24.996
one glass of wine at 8 pm
makes you a better mom.

00:00:24.996 --> 00:00:27.556
So pour yourself one and
let's talk about stuff.

00:00:27.556 --> 00:00:28.868
The best part is you don't even have

00:00:28.868 --> 00:00:30.644
to have kids to be a wine mom.

00:00:30.644 --> 00:00:33.849
We're gonna have some Chardonnay
that is the unofficial

00:00:33.849 --> 00:00:36.432
official wine of all wine moms.

00:00:37.767 --> 00:00:39.857
Okay, now I'm ready (laughs).

00:00:39.857 --> 00:00:41.250
Here's why I'm drinking tonight,

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:43.061
my son is obsessed with the movie that's

00:00:43.061 --> 00:00:45.264
out right now called BFG.

00:00:45.264 --> 00:00:48.097
But somehow in his four year old brain

00:00:48.097 --> 00:00:50.315
it's getting all scrambled
and my sister-in-law

00:00:50.315 --> 00:00:52.033
finally took him to see it on Sunday

00:00:52.033 --> 00:00:54.959
and come Monday I find out
that he's telling everyone,

00:00:54.959 --> 00:00:59.661
"Oh my auntie took me to
see CPS over the weekend."

00:00:59.661 --> 00:01:01.100
And for those of you who don't know

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:04.705
what CPS stands for it is
Child Protective Services.

00:01:04.705 --> 00:01:06.795
So now I have everybody thinking that

00:01:06.795 --> 00:01:09.709
my sister-in-law is taking my son to see

00:01:09.709 --> 00:01:13.876
Child Protective Services
because I am a terrible mother.

00:01:16.013 --> 00:01:17.941
So let's talk about the
best and worst things

00:01:17.941 --> 00:01:21.760
about having kids, kids
are the most beautiful

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:24.349
creatures on the planet
my kids are the most

00:01:24.349 --> 00:01:26.602
wonderful humans I've ever met in my life,

00:01:26.602 --> 00:01:28.287
that being said the first word

00:01:28.287 --> 00:01:31.294
that I think about when or no,

00:01:31.294 --> 00:01:34.193
so that being said the first
word that comes to mind

00:01:34.193 --> 00:01:36.968
when I think about parenting is shit.

00:01:36.968 --> 00:01:39.115
The first five or so years of your life

00:01:39.115 --> 00:01:40.915
you're being shit on literally--

00:01:40.915 --> 00:01:42.327
- [Voiceover] The first
years of their life.

00:01:42.327 --> 00:01:45.242
- Oh the first five or
so years of their life

00:01:45.242 --> 00:01:46.693
you're being shit on literally

00:01:46.693 --> 00:01:49.526
and then from there on out
you get shit on emotionally.

00:01:49.526 --> 00:01:51.500
I have a four year old and a one year old,

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:54.460
so I'm halfway through wiping two butts.

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:56.063
Then when it finally comes time to wipe

00:01:56.063 --> 00:01:58.724
your own butt you don't
even get to do that alone,

00:01:58.724 --> 00:02:01.228
my four year old likes to sit and watch me

00:02:01.228 --> 00:02:03.692
actually both of them
like to sit and watch me.

00:02:03.692 --> 00:02:05.701
And then when I say I'd like some privacy

00:02:05.701 --> 00:02:07.721
my four year old will go, "Oh okay."

00:02:07.721 --> 00:02:09.614
He'll shoo the one year old out,

00:02:09.614 --> 00:02:11.343
close the door, and sit back down.

00:02:11.343 --> 00:02:12.609
Okay dude whatever.

00:02:12.609 --> 00:02:15.233
But shit is not the only bodily fluid that

00:02:15.233 --> 00:02:17.044
comes out of these kids
there's just so much

00:02:17.044 --> 00:02:20.318
wetness like my kids
think that I want them

00:02:20.318 --> 00:02:23.395
to hand me their boogers, okay.

00:02:23.395 --> 00:02:26.761
And then when they vomit it's like

00:02:26.761 --> 00:02:30.535
they go out of their way to
vomit on something important.

00:02:30.535 --> 00:02:33.077
So my son will run out onto the couch

00:02:33.077 --> 00:02:35.457
to vomit on this fabric couch.

00:02:35.457 --> 00:02:37.965
You were in the bathroom, why, how?

00:02:37.965 --> 00:02:41.017
But even when they're doing
that I'm proud of them.

00:02:41.017 --> 00:02:43.362
Even when they puke everywhere
and I'm cleaning this up

00:02:43.362 --> 00:02:46.764
I'm like needy in vomit,
knee-deep in vomit.

00:02:46.764 --> 00:02:48.726
I'm like I am proud of you because I see

00:02:48.726 --> 00:02:50.084
that you ate your whole dinner,

00:02:50.084 --> 00:02:53.985
I see broccoli in here,
you ate some veggies, nice.

00:02:53.985 --> 00:02:57.526
So next (laughs).

00:02:57.526 --> 00:03:00.069
I can't be drunk because
it's just one glass

00:03:00.069 --> 00:03:04.069
I'm not even done so, I'm
just, this is just me.

00:03:04.991 --> 00:03:08.207
Next, so when you have
kids you become accustomed

00:03:08.207 --> 00:03:09.682
to constant noise it's like you

00:03:09.682 --> 00:03:11.980
kind of train yourself to zone it out.

00:03:11.980 --> 00:03:14.179
Once you finally get your silence,

00:03:14.179 --> 00:03:16.397
(crickets chirping)

00:03:16.397 --> 00:03:18.846
it's terrifying, something
terrible is happening,

00:03:18.846 --> 00:03:20.565
there is poop on the walls for sure.

00:03:20.565 --> 00:03:23.711
There's crayon on something,
someone's eating my lipstick.

00:03:23.711 --> 00:03:27.426
So one time it was silent and
my son was in the bathroom

00:03:27.426 --> 00:03:30.521
dunking the bath towels into the toilet

00:03:30.521 --> 00:03:33.528
and then sucking on them,
why would you do that?

00:03:33.528 --> 00:03:34.852
Are you thirsty?

00:03:34.852 --> 00:03:36.152
Does it taste good?

00:03:36.152 --> 00:03:38.555
Is there something I'm missing
about this toilet water?

00:03:38.555 --> 00:03:41.388
So you can't win, you
finally get your silence

00:03:41.388 --> 00:03:42.846
and it's awful.

00:03:42.846 --> 00:03:43.679
Hold on.

00:03:45.089 --> 00:03:47.162
Just a little bit more.

00:03:47.162 --> 00:03:48.393
That was a really small glass

00:03:48.393 --> 00:03:50.254
that I poured myself at first.

00:03:50.254 --> 00:03:54.038
Next, the cost kids are so expensive.

00:03:54.038 --> 00:03:57.835
There's swim lessons, there's
new shoes every other week,

00:03:57.835 --> 00:04:00.412
their feet grow so fast,
I don't understand how.

00:04:00.412 --> 00:04:01.643
It's like hobbits.

00:04:01.643 --> 00:04:03.245
They just like take and take and take

00:04:03.245 --> 00:04:06.183
all your money and then they
don't even appreciate it.

00:04:06.183 --> 00:04:08.644
Like my son eats all organic.

00:04:08.644 --> 00:04:11.674
I spend all this extra money
buying him organic food.

00:04:11.674 --> 00:04:15.621
So I make him his organic
bread, turkey, sandwich

00:04:15.621 --> 00:04:17.560
he'll ask for the crust to be cut off.

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:19.743
So the other morning I cut the crust off

00:04:19.743 --> 00:04:21.334
then all of the sudden he decided

00:04:21.334 --> 00:04:22.893
in that time I was cutting the crust

00:04:22.893 --> 00:04:25.970
that he doesn't want the
crust cut off anymore.

00:04:25.970 --> 00:04:28.629
So I serve him the sandwich and he's like,

00:04:28.629 --> 00:04:29.581
"Oh my God, Mom."

00:04:29.581 --> 00:04:32.622
Meltdown, flop on the floor wiggle around.

00:04:32.622 --> 00:04:35.049
So I take the crust and
I'm like shoving them

00:04:35.049 --> 00:04:37.301
like squeezing them
trying to get the mustard

00:04:37.301 --> 00:04:39.600
to like stick them back on.

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:41.318
But no that's not gonna do,

00:04:41.318 --> 00:04:43.408
he doesn't even want to
see the crust anymore

00:04:43.408 --> 00:04:45.266
it's too traumatizing for him.

00:04:45.266 --> 00:04:46.903
So I eat them because that's pretty much

00:04:46.903 --> 00:04:48.551
the lunch I have these days.

00:04:48.551 --> 00:04:50.397
How dare you Mom for eating my crust,

00:04:50.397 --> 00:04:52.452
I actually wanted it all along.

00:04:52.452 --> 00:04:54.623
You can't win (laughs).

00:04:54.623 --> 00:04:56.806
And finally, why?

00:04:56.806 --> 00:04:58.524
Your child is going to ask, "Why?"

00:04:58.524 --> 00:05:00.870
To every mundane little thing you say.

00:05:00.870 --> 00:05:03.133
That grass is green, "Why?"

00:05:03.133 --> 00:05:05.107
Because of chlorophyll, "Why?"

00:05:05.107 --> 00:05:07.336
I don't remember eighth grade biology,

00:05:07.336 --> 00:05:11.075
and it makes realize how little
you know about the world.

00:05:11.075 --> 00:05:14.992
But on the other hand
you have this opportunity

00:05:15.963 --> 00:05:19.863
and this chance to make
something beautiful.

00:05:19.863 --> 00:05:23.486
It's basically like
learning from your life

00:05:23.486 --> 00:05:25.831
and making something
better for somebody else.

00:05:25.831 --> 00:05:27.422
I can't think of something that holds

00:05:27.422 --> 00:05:29.755
any more meaning than that.

00:05:29.755 --> 00:05:34.062
All I can hope is that I
don't fuck it up (laughs).

00:05:34.062 --> 00:05:37.487
So that's all for now,
I have about two sips

00:05:37.487 --> 00:05:40.987
left of this and that's my cue to lay down

00:05:41.969 --> 00:05:45.661
and melt into the couch
with a nice crappy TV show.

00:05:45.661 --> 00:05:49.321
Until next time, I'm Hannah
your neighborhood wine mom,

00:05:49.321 --> 00:05:51.317
and I'll see you later.

00:05:51.317 --> 00:05:54.650
You won't want to see me like this, go.

00:05:57.517 --> 00:05:58.767
My mom never...

00:06:00.441 --> 00:06:02.206
punished me for burping,

00:06:02.206 --> 00:06:05.408
that was like the one thing
that she didn't think was rude.

